   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the village of Northport, in Suffolk county, to hire a village\nclerk or deputy clerk who is not a resident of such village",
    "basePrintNo": "S1787",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1787-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3-300, Vil L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1787    REVISED 01/19/2021\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation\nto authorizing the village of Northport, in Suffolk county, to hire a\nvillage clerk or deputy clerk who is not a resident of such village\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorizes the village of Northport, in Suffolk county, to hire a\nvillage clerk and deputy clerk who are not a resident of such village.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1: Amends Section 3-300 of the village law to add a new subdivi-\nsion allowing the village of Northport, Suffolk County to hire persons\nto fill the position of clerk and deputy clerk, who are not residents of\nthe village\n\nSECTION 2: Amends section 3 the public officer's law to add a new subdi-\nvision allowing a person who is not a resident of the village of North-\nport, Suffolk County to fill and perform the functions and duties of\nvillage clerk and deputy village clerk.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Village of Northport has requested this special legislation which\nwould allow them to hire a Village Clerk and Deputy Clerk who reside\noutside the geographic boundaries of the Village of Northport.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
